<title>SOUTH AFRICA: NEW REPUBLIC BANK HALF YEAR SHR SLIPS.</title>
<headline>NEW REPUBLIC BANK HALF YEAR SHR SLIPS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     8.2	   vs 24.1</p>
<p>    Fully Diluted shr (cts) 10.5	vs 23.2</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2.81	  vs 7.03</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   3.36	  vs 8.58</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.55	  vs 1.56</p>
<p>    Net interest income   18.99	 vs 21.09</p>
<p>Full name: New Republic Bank Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said that its results had been achieved</p>
<p>against a background of narrowing interest margins and</p>
<p>disruption caused by an extensive reorganisation of the group</p>
<p>following a change in owenership in March.</p>
<p>The bank is now controlled by Malaysian entrepeneur</p>
<p>Dato'Samsudin Abu Hassan.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
